+# Missing results histograms — 2026-10-09
+
+Requirements: R01/R03, RR06, TD06/TD08, B05/B07 and Q01. The owner reports that the normal race-complete page shows “Comparison unavailable” despite artificial drivers having created comparison records.
+
+The owner-authorized development rollout is complete. Both live Underpass histograms now return **200** with 101 distinct drivers; all 27 eligible tracks, native packet acceptance and the deployment smoke pass.
+
+The initial live development API lacked `GET /v1/track-versions/{version_id}/results-comparison`. Its public OpenAPI document omitted that route and the authenticated Underpass request returned **404**. Artificial drivers were enabled. The existing private histogram for Underpass, Compact, already contained **100 verified driver PBs** and eight bins. The cause was the missing backend rollout, not a lack of data. [Sanitized initial observation](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/live-underpass.json).
+
+## Prepared correction
+
+A local image, `bmt-results-endpoint:20261009`, derives from the exact live parent `925c6b2606395012a8d9c85a01ac46918fc1f8b44b4b9a88927f111ee7a3ca50`. Exact function/import replacements modify only `runs.py`, `test_drivers.py` and `cloud_smoke.py`. The image contains the existing reviewed unified histogram implementation: one driver contribution across compatible real/development boards, verified race PBs, best verified flying laps, exact bins and current-result placement. Existing public competitive/rating/eligibility isolation remains. No population selector or diagnostic caption is added to the game.
+
+All **112 packaged canonical-game files are byte-identical** to the parent; schema remains unchanged and no migration/reseed is required. The image imports the actual patched `/app/bmt_backend` modules and verifies that the results endpoint exposes the parameters the client uses. [Packaged game hashes/proof](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/packaged-game-proof.json), [preparation receipt](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/preparation.json).
+
+`backend/bmt_backend/cloud_smoke.py` now rejects missing/incompatible comparison routes, so native replay/storage/schema success alone cannot conceal this client/server mismatch. `backend/tests/test_results_deployment.py` covers the actual app, a missing endpoint and an older endpoint lacking the required parameters. The existing development smoke job must use the derived image for this check to take effect.
+
+The reviewed runtime histogram implementations are already present in the workspace; no additional client or canonical simulation change was needed. Private preparation/extraction helpers and the exact replacement context are under `.tools/results-endpoint-20261009`, outside the export root. The prepared overlay cherry-picks the histogram and smoke changes onto the live backend; it excludes other pending backend work.
+
+## Actual commands and outcomes
+
+- HTTPS `GET /v1/bootstrap`, `/openapi.json` and `/v1/track-versions/.../results-comparison?vehicle_id=compact`: bootstrap 200/artificial drivers enabled; OpenAPI 200/route absent; comparison 404. Requests use the established local TLS trust file.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe .tools/results-endpoint-20261009/inspect_live.py`: authenticated existing artificial-profile session; Underpass private histogram **100 PBs**, result comparison **404**. No races, track uploads, new driver profiles or player-record changes. The first fixed-developer diagnostic login returned `USERNAME_TAKEN`; the existing artificial profile avoided changing that account.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe .tools/results-endpoint-20261009/prepare.py`: exact live-base replacements and Python compilation pass; three files, no schema/canonical change.
+- `wsl.exe -d Ubuntu --cd '/mnt/c/Codes/Godot/Beat my track/.tools/results-endpoint-20261009' -- docker build --pull=false --network=none --platform=linux/amd64 --tag bmt-results-endpoint:20261009 .`: local build passes. Initial build imported the unpatched installed package; explicitly selecting `/app` corrected the build-time verification. The successful check imports `/app/bmt_backend/runs.py`. This preparation step performed no registry upload; the later authorized upload is recorded below.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest backend/tests/test_results_deployment.py backend/tests/test_domains.py backend/tests/test_test_drivers.py -q -k '(histogram or results_comparison or deployment_check or comparison_contract) and not postgres' --tb=short --show-capture=no`: **9 passed, 65 deselected** against SQLite. Same command against the three exact packaged modules in an isolated package copy: **9 passed, 65 deselected**. [Workspace results](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/backend-tests.xml), [packaged-module results](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/packaged-backend-tests.xml). PostgreSQL was explicitly excluded; remaining supporting modules in the isolated package copy use current workspace sources.
+- `powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_results_histograms.gd -Graphical`, isolated `APPDATA=build/results-endpoint-user` and dated `BMT_RESULTS_EVIDENCE`: **49 checks, zero failures**. Uses pinned Godot 4.7.2 ed1daf0bf. Earlier sandbox-only attempt failed to read Windows root certificates; the permitted runtime rerun passed.
+- Ruff on `cloud_smoke.py` and `test_results_deployment.py`, scoped `git diff --check`: pass.
+
+Native captures show both histograms, current race/PB markers and usable charts at 1280×720, 960×540 and 1600×720. [Compact capture, inspected](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/comparison-960x540.png). The capture uses retained canonical Silmukka driver data and illustrative player times from the existing fixture; it is not a new live Underpass finish. [Fixture provenance](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/verified-silmukka-histograms.json).
+
+## Completed development deployment
+
+The owner explicitly authorized updating the backend after reviewing the prepared correction. The tested image was uploaded to the existing retained `beat-my-track` development Artifact Registry repository `europe-west1-docker.pkg.dev/beat-my-track/bmt-stg-e7a444ab-images/backend`. The API, worker and smoke/migrate/catalog job images now use immutable digest `a00d8aede0a2e73e8f3d9ca2377e134b1dcdd0bc756e820173e4a13750c4ad18`. Live ownership/parent guards passed, and fresh Cloud SQL backup **1791570217827** completed successfully before upload/rollout. No migration or reseed was run. Existing data, development gates and canonical files remain intact. [Deployment receipt](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/deployment.json), [exact backend image patch](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/backend-image.patch).
+
+Actual authorized commands: `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe .tools/results-endpoint-20261009/deploy.py backup`, then `publish`, `deploy`, `smoke`; `verify_live.py`; and `audit.py`. All completed successfully. The API and worker report **Ready** on the intended image. The smoke job's actual logged result includes `results_comparison_route: true`, schema `0020_challenges`, **12,757 canonical ticks**, two temporary diagnostic storage objects and **zero player writes**. [Actual readiness/smoke result](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/final-readiness.json).
+
+Live combined race/lap responses pass across **all 27 tracks** in the current eligible development catalog. Underpass returns HTTP **200**, **101 distinct drivers** for each metric, including the retained **100 artificial PBs**, and eight bins for each metric. The private board remains inaccessible through the public histogram route (404). Candidate race/lap placement, metric/board consistency and exact bin totals pass. No races were generated/submitted or player records changed. [Underpass response](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/live-underpass-after.json), [all-track checks](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/live-catalog-checks.json).
+
+`game/tests/test_results_histograms.gd` now accepts optional `BMT_LIVE_RESULTS_PACKET` evidence, exercising the actual deployed packet through `RaceComplete._apply_comparison`, every driver count, the owner's displayed result markers and stable repeated reads. The owner's screenshot times are explicitly UI fixtures; no lap splits or verified race are invented/submitted. Pinned `scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_results_histograms.gd` with `BMT_LIVE_RESULTS_PACKET=.../live-underpass-after.json` and isolated `APPDATA`: **43 checks, zero failures**, headless. [Native log](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/native-live-packet.log).
+
+The earlier upload approval rejection was resolved by the owner's explicit authorization; no further permission was requested. No production deployment, schema migration, reseed or player-record mutation was performed. No phone attachment check or physical-device test was performed. No Android export/install, PostgreSQL/full regression or full `Validate` was run. Remaining acceptance: owner/device visual review while reopening the normal race-complete page; the live backend and native packet acceptance are verified. [Task-only review patch](evidence/results-endpoint-2026-10-09/scoped-change.patch) preserves unrelated workspace work.
